# Switch the tricycle controller's exact mode: while enabled, traction is held
# until the steering error is below the threshold (instead of scaling down with
# the error as in normal driving).
bool enable
# Steering error [rad] below which traction is released while exact mode is
# enabled. 0.0 (unset) selects the controller's exact_mode_threshold parameter.
# Valid range (0, pi].
float64 threshold
# While exact mode is enabled: a turn on the spot (v == 0, w != 0) keeps the
# wheel on the +-90 deg side it already stands on (last steering command) and
# reverses traction for the other turn direction, instead of the spin rule's
# +90 deg for w > 0 / -90 deg for w < 0 (a lock-to-lock swing of ~180 deg,
# 3-4.5 s, at a spin start or a retry). A wheel within 0.1 rad of straight
# has no side to keep. Cleared with exact mode.
bool keep_wheel_side
---
bool success
string message
